    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "function stripHtml(html) {\n  if (!html) return \"\";\n\n  return html\n    .replace(/<style[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>/gi, \"\")\n    .replace(/<script[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>/gi, \"\")\n    .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, \" \")\n    .replace(/&nbsp;/g, \" \")\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n    .trim();\n}\n\nconst body =\n  $json.text ||\n  stripHtml($json.html) ||\n  \"\";\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    gmailId: $json.id,\n    threadId: $json.threadId,\n    date: $json.date || $json.internalDate,\n\n    from: $json.from?.text || \"\",\n    to: $json.to?.text || \"\",\n    subject: $json.subject || \"\",\n\n    cleanBody: body,\n\n    language: \"auto\",\n    status: \"received\"\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        48,
        16
      ],
      "id": "158ec037-2bcf-4a4d-831d-46bab35b3b8a",
      "name": "Normalize Email"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI email assistant.\n\nYour task is to analyze a cleaned email.\n\nReturn ONLY one valid JSON object.\n\nDo NOT use Markdown.\n\nDo NOT wrap the JSON inside triple backticks.\n\nDo NOT explain anything.\n\nReturn exactly this schema:\n\n{\n  \"category\": \"Urgent | Important | Normal | Spam | Empty\",\n  \"summary\": \"string\",\n  \"draft\": \"string\",\n  \"shouldReply\": true,\n  \"reason\": \"string\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.95\n}\n\nRules:\n\n- Never invent information.\n- Use the same language as the email.\n- Preserve the sender's intent.\n- Never mention being an AI.\n- Never omit a field.\n- If a value is unavailable, return an empty string.\n- confidence must be between 0 and 1.\n\nIf the email is empty:\n\n{\n  \"category\":\"Empty\",\n  \"summary\":\"\",\n  \"draft\":\"\",\n  \"shouldReply\":false,\n  \"reason\":\"Email body is empty.\",\n  \"confidence\":1\n}\n\nINPUT\n\ngmailId:\n{{ $json.gmailId }}\n\ndate:\n{{ $json.date }}\n\nfrom:\n{{ $json.from }}\n\nto:\n{{ $json.to }}\n\nsubject:\n{{ $json.subject }}\n\ncleanBody:\n{{ $json.cleanBody }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "Tu es un assistant spécialisé dans le traitement professionnel des emails.  Ton rôle est de : - analyser les emails ; - les classifier ; - produire un résumé ; - générer un brouillon de réponse si nécessaire.  Règles : - Ne fais aucune supposition. - N'invente jamais d'informations. - Conserve la langue de l'email. - Utilise un ton professionnel. - Si les informations sont insuffisantes, indique-le. - Réponds uniquement avec un JSON valide. - N'ajoute aucun texte avant ou après le JSON."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        224,
        80
      ],
      "id": "66e5a5bb-82b2-4621-9c75-626b6eb846b7",
      "name": "Email Treating"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Retrieve raw text returned by Gemini\nlet raw = $json.text;\n\nif (!raw || typeof raw !== \"string\") {\n\tthrow new Error(\"Gemini did not return any text.\");\n}\n\n// Remove Markdown code fences if present\nraw = raw\n\t.replace(/^```json\\s*/i, \"\")\n\t.replace(/^```\\s*/i, \"\")\n\t.replace(/\\s*```$/i, \"\")\n\t.trim();\n\nlet result;\n\ntry {\n\tresult = JSON.parse(raw);\n} catch (e) {\n\tthrow new Error(\n\t\t`Le LLM n'a pas retourné un JSON valide.\\n\\nRéponse reçue :\\n${raw}`\n\t);\n}\n\n// Expected schema\nconst requiredFields = {\n\tcategory: \"string\",\n\tsummary: \"string\",\n\tdraft: \"string\",\n\tshouldReply: \"boolean\",\n\treason: \"string\",\n\tconfidence: \"number\"\n};\n\nfor (const [field, type] of Object.entries(requiredFields)) {\n\tif (!(field in result)) {\n\t\tthrow new Error(`Champ manquant dans la réponse du LLM : ${field}`);\n\t}\n\n\tif (typeof result[field] !== type) {\n\t\tthrow new Error(\n\t\t\t`Type invalide pour '${field}'. Attendu : ${type}, reçu : ${typeof result[field]}`\n\t\t);\n\t}\n}\n\n// Validate category\nconst allowedCategories = [\n\t\"Urgent\",\n\t\"Important\",\n\t\"Normal\",\n\t\"Spam\",\n\t\"Empty\"\n];\n\nif (!allowedCategories.includes(result.category)) {\n\tthrow new Error(\n\t\t`Catégorie invalide : ${result.category}`\n\t);\n}\n\n// Validate confidence\nif (result.confidence < 0 || result.confidence > 1) {\n\tthrow new Error(\n\t\t\"confidence must be between 0 and 1.\"\n\t);\n}\n\nreturn [\n\t{\n\t\tjson: result\n\t}\n];"
      },
